===Water birds===

[[File:Bird's Eggs from Sea-Cliffs tail-piece in Bewick British Birds 1804.jpg |thumb |220px |Bird's eggs from sea-cliffs: uncaptioned tail-piece in Volume 2: ''Water Birds''. Bewick has chosen a seabird theme, but humans are closely involved, and the birds are a useful resource.]]
The second volume "containing the History and Description of Water Birds" begins with its own preface, and its own introduction. Bewick discusses the question of where many seabirds go to breed, revisits the subject of migration, and concludes with reflections on "an all-wise Providence" as shown in Nature.

[[File:Heron woodcut Bewick's British Birds 1847.jpg |thumb |left |"The Heron. Common Heron, Heronsewgh, or Heronshaw. (''[[Ardea cinerea]]'', [[John Latham (ornithologist) |Lath]].—''Héron cendré'', [[Temminck |Temm]].)" woodcut]]

